WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:04.317
An unreleased concept site for manufacturing software:

2
00:00:04.317 --> 00:00:08.268
scroll through a 3D factory and watch it come to life.

3
00:00:08.268 --> 00:00:10.975
I built it alone in about five weeks.

4
00:00:11.867 --> 00:00:14.587
The 3D world is a plain TypeScript class.

5
00:00:14.587 --> 00:00:17.109
Angular only starts it in the browser,

6
00:00:17.109 --> 00:00:19.763
and cleans everything up when you leave.

7
00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:24.125
The camera follows a curved path at a steady speed,

8
00:00:24.125 --> 00:00:27.651
using a table of one thousand and twenty-four steps.

9
00:00:28.567 --> 00:00:31.398
The robot is built entirely in code:

10
00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:33.521
named joints, a walk cycle,

11
00:00:33.521 --> 00:00:37.375
and poses like pulling a lever or carrying boxes.

12
00:00:38.267 --> 00:00:43.173
Switching lights on and off caused stalls of up to two hundred milliseconds,

13
00:00:43.173 --> 00:00:46.595
so the lights now stay in the scene and fade instead.

14
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:51.100
It was never released, and the case study says so.

15
00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:53.044
The details are on my site.

